      {
        "id": 47402,
        "name": "LCinn",
        "username": "LCinn",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lcinn/{size}/2659_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-30T10:18:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Technically, what Ameena does is not the `correct' way to play, but personally I find it a much more enjoyable way. Officially it's about the order the cards were played, which is a pain to keep track of between decks, and, as TheJayMann says, even then the answer isn't entirely clear.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My advice: play as Ameena does, it plays smoother. Sure, it'll give you the advantage at times, but it won't happen often, and when it happens, the alternative feels a bit artificial. Perhaps try to keep track of the situations where it would be relevant, and see if you prefer one style or the other.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:20:53.209Z",
