        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Technically, what Ameena does is not the `correct&#39; way to play, but personally I find it a much more enjoyable way. Officially it&#39;s about the order the cards were played, which is a pain to keep track of between decks, and, as TheJayMann says, even then the answer isn&#39;t entirely clear.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My advice: play as Ameena does, it plays smoother. Sure, it&#39;ll give you the advantage at times, but it won&#39;t happen often, and when it happens, the alternative feels a bit artificial. Perhaps try to keep track of the situations where it would be relevant, and see if you prefer one style or the other.</p>",
