      {
        "id": 47403,
        "name": "Koga",
        "username": "Koga",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/{size}/2058_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-30T14:28:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Could also think about it in a \"thematic\" way. Which would reduce damage first, some shielding winds blocking the damage from reaching you, or Legacy's bulletproof skin (Fortitude) once the damage reaches you? One would think a shield&nbsp;reduces damage before skin. The thing is also the wording, Shielding Winds says \"would be dealt damage\" and both Ta Moko and Fortitude say \"damage dealt\", so it depends if those 2 wordings act in a certain order or not. I'm not sure if we've ever gotten an official ruling or not about this.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:20:53.299Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
